WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.762
Branch order matters when CASE conditions overlap If
age greater than or

00:00:04.788 --> 00:00:09.112
equal to eighteen comes first every senior also
satisfies that condition so

00:00:09.125 --> 00:00:13.100
the senior branch can never run The correct order
places the more

00:00:13.125 --> 00:00:18.588
specific senior threshold first then the broader
adult threshold Run both versions

00:00:18.612 --> 00:00:23.050
and inspect the classifications for the older
patients This is the same

00:00:23.075 --> 00:00:26.575
general rule you will use for billing tiers and
priority labels place

00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:32.438
specific or high-priority conditions before broad
conditions If one branch logically contains

00:00:32.450 --> 00:00:35.338
another the narrower branch normally needs to come
first
